{"step_index":152,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-05T09:51:45Z","input_tokens":2579,"cache_read_tokens":172765,"output_tokens":2228,"thinking":"Initial investigation reveals the environment creation command utilizes `micromamba` version `2.10.0`. It aims to create an environment at a specified prefix, installing a suite of scientific computing packages including Python 3.11, NumPy, SciPy, and others, along with build tools such as CMake and Make. The command's full intent appears to be setting up a development environment for scientific simulations.\n\n\nThe environment creation command encounters potential conflict due to differing dependency constraints for `qe`, `lammps`, and the scientific Python packages when combined in a single environment. Installing the Python packages via `pip` separately from `qe` might bypass this issue, as `pip` handles prebuilt wheels without conda's solver. Separate environment creation for `qe` and `lammps` could also avoid complex solver interactions, given the faster resolution time for individual packages.\n\n\nThe existing system setup includes essential build tools and Python already, which suggests that relying solely on `micromamba` for all packages might be unnecessary. Initial hypothesis: the script might be over-provisioning with conda packages when system binaries are available. Refactoring the environment creation involves installing a minimal base environment with `micromamba` (Python, qe, and cmake) followed by the required scientific Python packages using `pip`. Subsequently, building LAMMPS can leverage the system compilers and the newly created `cmake` in the environment.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"#!/bin/bash\\n# ==============================================================================\\n# setup_local_rtx5080_env.sh\\n# 新PC (Core Ultra 9 285K / RAM 64GB / RTX 5080 16GB / Windows 11 Pro WSL2) 用\\n# root権限 (sudo) 不要の高速セットアップスクリプト\\n# ==============================================================================\\nset -e\\n\\nSCRIPT_DIR=\\\"$(cd \\\"$(dirname \\\"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\\\")\\\" && pwd)\\\"\\nWORKSPACE_DIR=\\\"$(dirname \\\"$SCRIPT_DIR\\\")\\\"\\nENV_PREFIX=\\\"/home/WORKSTATION4WSL/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/mdi_env_rtx5080\\\"\\nMAMBA_ROOT=\\\"/home/WORKSTATION4WSL/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/micromamba\\\"\\nMAMBA_BIN=\\\"$MAMBA_ROOT/bin/micromamba\\\"\\nLOCAL_BIN=\\\"$SCRIPT_DIR/bin\\\"\\nmkdir -p \\\"$MAMBA_ROOT/bin\\\" \\\"$LOCAL_BIN\\\"\\n\\necho \\\"============================================================\\\"\\necho \\\" Step 1: Micromamba パッケージマネージャの確認 (sudo 不要)\\\"\\necho \\\"============================================================\\\"\\nif [ ! -x \\\"$MAMBA_BIN\\\" ]; then\\n    curl -Ls https://micro.mamba.pm/api/micromamba/linux-64/latest | tar -xvj -C \\\"$MAMBA_ROOT/bin\\\" --strip-components=1 bin/micromamba\\n    chmod +x \\\"$MAMBA_BIN\\\"\\nfi\\necho \\\"✅ Micromamba ready: $MAMBA_BIN\\\"\\n\\necho \\\"============================================================\\\"\\necho \\\" Step 2: Quantum ESPRESSO (pw.x) & Python 3.11 & CMake の高速導入\\\"\\necho \\\"============================================================\\\"\\nif [ ! -x \\\"$ENV_PREFIX/bin/pw.x\\\" ]; then\\n    rm -rf \\\"$ENV_PREFIX\\\"\\n    \\\"$MAMBA_BIN\\\" create -y -p \\\"$ENV_PREFIX\\\" -c conda-forge \\\\\\n        python=3.11 pip cmake qe\\nelse\\n    echo \\\"✅ Quantum ESPRESSO ($ENV_PREFIX/bin/pw.x) already installed.\\\"\\nfi\\n\\nexport PATH=\\\"$LOCAL_BIN:$ENV_PREFIX/bin:$PATH\\\"\\nexport LD_LIBRARY_PATH=\\\"$ENV_PREFIX/lib:${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:-}\\\"\\n\\necho \\\"============================================================\\\"\\necho \\\" Step 3: Python パッケージ (NumPy, SciPy, Matplotlib, ASE, PyMDI) の導入\\\"\\necho \\\"========================================\n<truncated 2319 bytes>","Overwrite":"true","Path":"\"/home/WORKSTATION4WSL/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/mdi_workspace_backup/c